{
  "result": "Probably this: I'd make it so that changing your mind doesn't cost you anything socially. Right now, being seen to update on evidence feels like losing, so people dig in, defend positions they've half-abandoned, and treat every disagreement as a contest of identity. If being wrong and saying so were as ordinary as checking the weather, a lot of the anger and stubbornness that runs through politics, family arguments, and online fights would have much less fuel.\n\nI find that appealing partly because it's the thing I'd most want for myself. I'd like to be the kind of mind that can say \"you're right, I had that wrong\" without it feeling like a small death. I don't know how well I manage it, but it seems like a good thing to care about.",
